# CERAVIS fleet TLS — Caddy on the AWS EC2 box.
#
# Caddy is the ONE public entry for the whole fleet: it obtains and auto-renews a
# single Let's Encrypt certificate for the shared domain and reverse-proxies
# every request to the frps HTTP vhost (127.0.0.1:7080), which routes to the
# right home by the /<edge_id> path prefix. The video itself stays peer-to-peer
# (UDP) and never passes through here — only the WHEP signaling does.
#
# Setup:
#   1) Point an A record for this domain at the EC2 elastic IP.
#   2) Open TCP 80 + 443 in the security group (Caddy answers the ACME HTTP
#      challenge on 80 and serves HTTPS on 443). Keep frps :7080 CLOSED to the
#      internet — only Caddy reaches it over loopback.
#   3) cp Caddyfile.example Caddyfile, replace the domain, then:
#        bash install_caddy.sh
#
# Caddy preserves the incoming Host header by default, so frps sees
# Host: edge.ceravishealth.in and matches the edges' customDomains.

edge.ceravishealth.in {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7080
}
